From d2fbdeb0984c6d506a8a8980aa82f6fca27868e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iimmyy <i.a.martins001@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:29:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/36] ggml-hexagon on v68: whole-brain NPU runs; Q2_K and
 Q4_0 in 32-row tiles

- v68 DSP dies on DMA writes from VTCM to DDR and on DMA started from the
  callback thread: write-backs are HVX copies (hex-dma.h), the binary-op
  row broadcast is an HVX copy. ADD/MUL/RMS_NORM/SCALE/ROPE now pass.
- Q2_K (new) and Q4_0 weights repacked into 32-row tiles; one contiguous
  DMA per tile, 32 rows per vector (no row reductions). Inputs quantized
  like the board CPU's q8_K / q8_0, in cached heap memory (scalar loads
  stall on VTCM).
- lg-trace.h: file trace for the DSP (off by default).
- test-backend-ops: Q2_K cases in Gemma 4 E4B shapes.
